IMPORT `wra3-pt4-s77-84`

-- wra3-pt6-misc.l4: the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Part 6 (Miscellaneous), sections 135 to 146.
-- Part wra3, layer 1. Written from inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk (version
-- 2026-07-01), not the official text.
--
-- Host Acts (not among the sources): RSA = Registration Service Act 1953; CSA = Child Support Act 1991; CMOPA = Child
-- Maintenance and Other Payments Act 2008; IA = Insolvency Act 1986; ETA = Employment and Training Act 1973;
-- BDRA = Births and Deaths Registration Act 1953. What a host Act's other sections say is a borrowed fact, asked as an input.
-- The terms "person with care", "non-resident parent" and "qualifying child" are Child Support Act 1991 terms: each is asked
-- as a fact, because the core has no type for them and this part needs none (no NEEDS-CORE.md was written).
--
-- Reading a result: JUST FALSE is the text's own "no"; NOTHING is "not covered" (silent, "includes", or limited by its own wording).

§ `s 135 Functions of registration service (Tell Us Once)`

-- RSA 19A(1): the functions of a registrar of births and deaths, a superintendent registrar and the Registrar General
-- include the power to transmit information from a declaration under BDRA 9(1) or a birth register entry to the Secretary
-- of State, and to verify it for the Secretary of State, for the purposes of the service in (2).
-- src:2480 | (1) The functions of a registrar of births and deaths, a superintendent registrar and the Registrar General include the power to—
-- src:2481 | (a) transmit information contained in a declaration made under section 9(1) of the Births and Deaths Registration Act 1953 or entered in a register of births to the Secretary of State, and
-- src:2482 | (b) verify such information for the Secretary of State,
-- src:2483 | for the purposes of the service in subsection (2).
@ref s 135 RSA 19A(1) (src:2480-2483)
GIVEN `the information is contained in a declaration made under section 9(1) of the Births and Deaths Registration Act 1953 or entered in a register of births` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transmission or verification is for the purposes of the service in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135 RSA 19A(1) the functions of a registrar include the power to transmit and verify the information for the Secretary of State` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the information is contained in a declaration made under section 9(1) of the Births and Deaths Registration Act 1953 or entered in a register of births`
           AND `the transmission or verification is for the purposes of the service in subsection (2)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The functions ... include the power to" the two named things for the named purposes; the text does not say what else is or is not within them
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- RSA 19A(2): That service is a service operated by the Secretary of State by which individuals may transmit information
-- about births to the Secretary of State, and that information may be transmitted to other persons by the Secretary of State.
-- src:2484 | (2) That service is a service operated by the Secretary of State by which—
-- src:2485 | (a) individuals may transmit information about births to the Secretary of State, and
-- src:2486 | (b) that information may be transmitted to other persons by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 135 RSA 19A(2) (src:2484-2486)
GIVEN `the service is operated by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `individuals may transmit information about births to the Secretary of State by it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that information may be transmitted to other persons by the Secretary of State by it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135 RSA 19A(2) the arrangement is the service in subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the service is operated by the Secretary of State`
           AND `individuals may transmit information about births to the Secretary of State by it`
           AND `that information may be transmitted to other persons by the Secretary of State by it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "That service is a service operated by ..." describes the service and does not say "means" or "only"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- RSA 19A(3): references to the Secretary of State include persons providing services to the Secretary of State for the purpose of that service.
-- src:2487 | (3) References in subsections (1) and (2) to the Secretary of State include persons providing services to the Secretary of State for the purpose of the service referred in subsection (2).
@ref s 135 RSA 19A(3) (src:2487)
GIVEN `the person provides services to the Secretary of State for the purpose of the service in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135 RSA 19A(3) the person is within the references to the Secretary of State in subsections (1) and (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person provides services to the Secretary of State for the purpose of the service in subsection (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References ... to the Secretary of State include" those persons; the text does not say who else is or is not within them
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- RSA 19A(4): This section does not authorise any disclosure which is unlawful by virtue of any enactment, or by reason of
-- the law relating to confidentiality or privacy.
-- src:2488 | (4) This section does not authorise any disclosure which is unlawful—
-- src:2489 | (a) by virtue of any enactment, or
-- src:2490 | (b) by reason of the law relating to confidentiality or privacy.
@ref s 135 RSA 19A(4) (src:2488-2490)
GIVEN `the disclosure is unlawful by virtue of any enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is unlawful by reason of the law relating to confidentiality or privacy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135 RSA 19A(4) the section authorises the disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not authorise any disclosure which is unlawful (a) by virtue of any enactment, or (b) by reason of the law relating to confidentiality or privacy"
        IF `the disclosure is unlawful by virtue of any enactment` OR `the disclosure is unlawful by reason of the law relating to confidentiality or privacy` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what the section does not authorise and does not say that it authorises anything else
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 136 Supporting maintenance agreements`

-- CSA 9(2A): with a view to reducing the need for applications under sections 4 and 7, the Secretary of State (a) may take
-- such steps as the Secretary of State considers appropriate to encourage the making and keeping of maintenance
-- agreements, and (b) in particular, before accepting an application under those sections, may invite the applicant to
-- consider with the Secretary of State whether it is possible to make such an agreement.
-- src:2493 | (1) In section 9 of the Child Support Act 1991 (maintenance agreements), after subsection (2) there is inserted—
-- src:2494 | (2A) The Secretary of State may, with a view to reducing the need for applications under sections 4 and 7—
-- src:2495 | (a) take such steps as the Secretary of State considers appropriate to encourage the making and keeping of maintenance agreements, and
-- src:2496 | (b) in particular, before accepting an application under those sections, invite the applicant to consider with the Secretary of State whether it is possible to make such an agreement.
@ref s 136(1) CSA 9(2A) (src:2493-2496)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State considers the step appropriate to encourage the making and keeping of maintenance agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(1) CSA 9(2A)(a) the Secretary of State may take the step` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary of State considers the step appropriate to encourage the making and keeping of maintenance agreements` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to take "such steps as the Secretary of State considers appropriate"; the text is silent on a step the Secretary of State does not consider appropriate
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 136(1) CSA 9(2A)(b) (src:2496)
GIVEN `the application under section 4 or 7 has been accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(1) CSA 9(2A)(b) the Secretary of State may invite the applicant to consider whether it is possible to make a maintenance agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application under section 4 or 7 has been accepted` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the invitation is "before accepting an application"; the text is silent on one made after acceptance
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- CMOPA Sch 5 para 3(3): the Secretary of State may, before accepting an application required by provision under
-- sub-paragraph (2)(b), invite the applicant to consider whether it is possible to make a maintenance agreement.
-- src:2497 | (2) In Schedule 5 to the Child Maintenance and Other Payments Act 2008 (maintenance calculations: transfer of cases to new rules), in paragraph 3, after sub-paragraph (2) there is inserted—
-- src:2498 | (3) The Secretary of State may before accepting an application required by provision under sub-paragraph (2)(b) invite the applicant to consider with the Secretary of State whether it is possible to make a maintenance agreement (within the meaning of section 9 of the Child Support Act 1991).
@ref s 136(2) CMOPA Sch 5 para 3(3) (src:2497-2498)
GIVEN `the application is an application required by provision under sub-paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application has been accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(2) CMOPA Sch 5 para 3(3) the Secretary of State may invite the applicant to consider whether it is possible to make a maintenance agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application is an application required by provision under sub-paragraph (2)(b)` AND (NOT `the application has been accepted`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the invitation is "before accepting an application required by provision under sub-paragraph (2)(b)"; the text is silent on any other
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 137 Collection of child support maintenance`

-- CSA 4(2A): The Secretary of State may only make arrangements under subsection (2)(a) if (a) the non-resident parent
-- agrees to the arrangements, or (b) the Secretary of State is satisfied that without them child support maintenance is
-- unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation.
-- src:2504 | (2A) The Secretary of State may only make arrangements under subsection (2)(a) if—
-- src:2505 | (a) the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements, or
-- src:2506 | (b) the Secretary of State is satisfied that without the arrangements child support maintenance is unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation.
@ref s 137(2) CSA 4(2A) (src:2504-2506)
GIVEN `the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that without the arrangements child support maintenance is unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 137(2) CSA 4(2A) the condition for arrangements under section 4(2)(a) is met` MEANS
    `the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements`
    OR `the Secretary of State is satisfied that without the arrangements child support maintenance is unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation`

@ref s 137(2) CSA 4(2A) (src:2504-2506)
GIVEN `the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that without the arrangements child support maintenance is unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(2) CSA 4(2A) the Secretary of State may make arrangements under section 4(2)(a)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 137(2) CSA 4(2A) the condition for arrangements under section 4(2)(a) is met` `the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that without the arrangements child support maintenance is unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation`
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "may only ... if" states a necessary condition; the power itself is in section 4(2)(a) of the Child Support Act 1991, which is not among the sources
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State may only make arrangements under subsection (2)(a) if (a) the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements, or (b) the Secretary of State is satisfied that ..."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- CSA 7(3A): the same condition for arrangements under section 7(3)(a) (a child in Scotland applying for a calculation).
-- src:2510 | (3A) The Secretary of State may only make arrangements under subsection (3)(a) if—
-- src:2511 | (a) the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements, or
-- src:2512 | (b) the Secretary of State is satisfied that without the arrangements child support maintenance is unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation.
@ref s 137(3) CSA 7(3A) (src:2510-2512)
GIVEN `the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that without the arrangements child support maintenance is unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 137(3) CSA 7(3A) the condition for arrangements under section 7(3)(a) is met` MEANS
    `the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements`
    OR `the Secretary of State is satisfied that without the arrangements child support maintenance is unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation`

@ref s 137(3) CSA 7(3A) (src:2510-2512)
GIVEN `the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that without the arrangements child support maintenance is unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(3) CSA 7(3A) the Secretary of State may make arrangements under section 7(3)(a)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 137(3) CSA 7(3A) the condition for arrangements under section 7(3)(a) is met` `the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that without the arrangements child support maintenance is unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation`
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "may only ... if" states a necessary condition; the power itself is in section 7(3)(a) of the Child Support Act 1991, which is not among the sources
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State may only make arrangements under subsection (3)(a) if (a) the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements, or (b) the Secretary of State is satisfied that ..."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- CSA 29(1): the power to collect is "(subject to section 4(2A) and 7(3A))". So an arrangement under 4(2)(a) or 7(3)(a)
-- is subject to the condition above, and any other collection is not touched by this amendment.
-- src:2513 | (4) In section 29 (collection of child support maintenance), in subsection (1), after “may” there is inserted “ (subject to section 4(2A) and 7(3A)) ”.
@ref s 137(4) CSA 29(1) (src:2513)
DECLARE `s 137(4) arrangement for collection` IS ONE OF
    `s 137(4) an arrangement under section 4(2)(a) of the Child Support Act 1991`
    `s 137(4) an arrangement under section 7(3)(a) of the Child Support Act 1991`
    `s 137(4) any other arrangement`

@ref s 137(4) CSA 29(1) (src:2513)
GIVEN `the arrangement` IS A `s 137(4) arrangement for collection`
      `the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that without the arrangements child support maintenance is unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(4) CSA 29(1) the Secretary of State may make the arrangement for collection, subject to sections 4(2A) and 7(3A)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the arrangement`
    WHEN `s 137(4) an arrangement under section 4(2)(a) of the Child Support Act 1991` THEN
        `s 137(2) CSA 4(2A) the Secretary of State may make arrangements under section 4(2)(a)` `the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that without the arrangements child support maintenance is unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation`
    WHEN `s 137(4) an arrangement under section 7(3)(a) of the Child Support Act 1991` THEN
        `s 137(3) CSA 7(3A) the Secretary of State may make arrangements under section 7(3)(a)` `the non-resident parent agrees to the arrangements` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that without the arrangements child support maintenance is unlikely to be paid in accordance with the calculation`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the amendment makes the power "subject to section 4(2A) and 7(3A)" only; it says nothing about any other arrangement
    WHEN `s 137(4) any other arrangement` THEN NOTHING

§ `s 138 Indicative maintenance calculations`

DECLARE `s 138 role in relation to a qualifying child` IS ONE OF
    `s 138 a person with care`
    `s 138 a non-resident parent`
    `s 138 neither a person with care nor a non-resident parent`

-- CSA 9A(1): a person with care or non-resident parent in relation to any qualifying child may apply to the Secretary of
-- State for an indicative calculation.
-- src:2517 | (1) A person with care or non-resident parent in relation to any qualifying child or qualifying children may apply to the Secretary of State for an indicative calculation with respect to that child or any of those children.
@ref s 138 CSA 9A(1) (src:2517)
GIVEN `the person's role in relation to the child` IS A `s 138 role in relation to a qualifying child`
      `the child is a qualifying child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138 CSA 9A(1) the person may apply for an indicative calculation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person's role in relation to the child`
    WHEN `s 138 a person with care` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to a person with care "in relation to any qualifying child"
        IF `the child is a qualifying child` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `s 138 a non-resident parent` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to a non-resident parent "in relation to any qualifying child"
        IF `the child is a qualifying child` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection grants the right to those two and does not say that anyone else may not apply
    WHEN `s 138 neither a person with care nor a non-resident parent` THEN NOTHING

-- CSA 9A(2): a qualifying child who has attained the age of 12 years and is habitually resident in Scotland may apply for
-- an indicative calculation with respect to themselves.
-- src:2518 | (2) A qualifying child who has attained the age of 12 years and is habitually resident in Scotland may apply to the Secretary of State for an indicative calculation with respect to himself or herself.
@ref s 138 CSA 9A(2) (src:2518)
GIVEN `the child` IS A Person
      `the child is a qualifying child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is habitually resident in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138 CSA 9A(2) the child may apply for an indicative calculation with respect to themselves` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the child is a qualifying child` AND `the child`'s `age in years` AT LEAST 12 AND `the child is habitually resident in Scotland` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to "A qualifying child who has attained the age of 12 years and is habitually resident in Scotland"; the text is silent on any other child
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- CSA 9A(3): an indicative calculation is a calculation of the amount of child support maintenance which the Secretary of
-- State considers would in accordance with section 11 be fixed by a maintenance calculation if one were made.
-- src:2519 | (3) An indicative calculation is a calculation of the amount of child support maintenance which the Secretary of State considers would in accordance with section 11 be fixed by a maintenance calculation if such a calculation were made with respect to the child or children in question.
@ref s 138 CSA 9A(3) (src:2519)
GIVEN `the calculation is of the amount of child support maintenance which the Secretary of State considers would in accordance with section 11 be fixed by a maintenance calculation if such a calculation were made with respect to the child or children in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138 CSA 9A(3) the calculation is an indicative calculation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the calculation is of the amount of child support maintenance which the Secretary of State considers would in accordance with section 11 be fixed by a maintenance calculation if such a calculation were made with respect to the child or children in question` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "An indicative calculation is a calculation of" is not "means" or "only", so the text does not say a calculation of another kind is not one
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- CSA 9A(4): An indicative calculation does not create any liability on any person to pay child support maintenance.
-- src:2520 | (4) An indicative calculation does not create any liability on any person to pay child support maintenance.
@ref s 138 CSA 9A(4) (src:2520)
GIVEN `the calculation is an indicative calculation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138 CSA 9A(4) the calculation creates a liability to pay child support maintenance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An indicative calculation does not create any liability on any person to pay child support maintenance"
        IF `the calculation is an indicative calculation` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection is about an indicative calculation only
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- CSA 9A(5): the Secretary of State may limit the number of applications the Secretary of State will accept in any
-- particular case, in such manner as the Secretary of State thinks fit.
-- src:2521 | (5) The Secretary of State may limit the number of applications the Secretary of State will accept under this section in any particular case in such manner as the Secretary of State thinks fit.
@ref s 138 CSA 9A(5) (src:2521)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has set a limit on the number of applications in this case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limit the Secretary of State has set` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of applications already accepted in this case` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138 CSA 9A(5) the application is not barred by a limit on the number of applications` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Secretary of State has set a limit on the number of applications in this case` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the number of applications already accepted in this case` LESS THAN `the limit the Secretary of State has set` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the limit is set "in such manner as the Secretary of State thinks fit", so what happens at the limit is not stated (a lawyer's reading (b); the other reading is JUST FALSE)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- CSA 9A(6): where the person alleged to be the parent denies being one of the child's parents, the Secretary of State
-- shall not make the indicative calculation on the assumption that the person is one of the parents unless the case falls
-- within paragraph (b) of Case A3 in section 26(2).
-- src:2522 | (6) Where a person who is alleged to be the parent of a child with respect to whom an application for an indicative calculation has been made denies being one of the child's parents, the Secretary of State shall not make the indicative calculation on the assumption that the person is one of the child's parents unless the case falls within paragraph (b) of Case A3 in section 26(2).
@ref s 138 CSA 9A(6) (src:2522)
GIVEN `the person alleged to be the parent denies being one of the child's parents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case falls within paragraph (b) of Case A3 in section 26(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138 CSA 9A(6) the Secretary of State is not barred from making the calculation on the assumption that the person is a parent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person alleged to be the parent denies being one of the child's parents` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the case falls within paragraph (b) of Case A3 in section 26(2)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Secretary of State shall not make the indicative calculation on the assumption that the person is one of the child's parents unless the case falls within paragraph (b) of Case A3 in section 26(2)"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `s 139 Recovery of child support maintenance by deduction from benefit`

-- CSA 43(1)-(2): the power to make regulations under section 5 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 by virtue of
-- subsection (1)(p) may be exercised with a view to securing payments of child support maintenance by a non-resident
-- parent, which includes the recovery of arrears and of fees payable under section 6 of the Child Maintenance and Other
-- Payments Act 2008.
-- src:2525 | (1) The power of the Secretary of State to make regulations under section 5 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 by virtue of subsection (1)(p) of that section may be exercised with a view to securing the making of payments in respect of child support maintenance by a non-resident parent.
-- src:2526 | (2) The reference in subsection (1) to the making of payments in respect of child support maintenance includes the recovery of—
-- src:2527 | (a) arrears of child support maintenance, and
-- src:2528 | (b) fees payable under section 6 of the Child Maintenance and Other Payments Act 2008.
@ref s 139 CSA 43(1)-(2) (src:2525-2528)
DECLARE `s 139 payment` IS ONE OF
    `s 139 a payment in respect of child support maintenance by a non-resident parent`
    `s 139 arrears of child support maintenance`
    `s 139 fees payable under section 6 of the Child Maintenance and Other Payments Act 2008`
    `s 139 any other payment`

@ref s 139 CSA 43(1)-(2) (src:2525-2528)
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `s 139 payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139 CSA 43 the regulations power under section 5(1)(p) of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 may be exercised to secure the payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `s 139 a payment in respect of child support maintenance by a non-resident parent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 139 arrears of child support maintenance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 139 fees payable under section 6 of the Child Maintenance and Other Payments Act 2008` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the making of payments in respect of child support maintenance includes" arrears and fees; the text does not say what else is or is not within it
    WHEN `s 139 any other payment` THEN NOTHING

§ `s 141 Review of fees regulations`

-- CMOPA 6(3A)-(3B): the Secretary of State must review the effect of the first regulations made under subsection (1)
-- before the end of the period of 30 months beginning with the day they come into force. This is the Secretary of State's
-- duty to Parliament and to nobody else; no seat is built on it.
-- src:2537 | (3A) The Secretary of State must review the effect of the first regulations made under subsection (1).
-- src:2538 | (3B) The review must take place before the end of the period of 30 months beginning with the day on which those regulations come into force.
@ref s 141 CMOPA 6(3A)-(3B) (src:2537-2538)
GIVEN `the day on which the first fees regulations come into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 141 CMOPA 6(3B) the last day of the 30 months beginning with the day the first fees regulations come into force` MEANS
    `s 81(3) the last day of the months beginning with the day` `the day on which the first fees regulations come into force` 30

@ref s 141 CMOPA 6(3A)-(3B) (src:2537-2538)
GIVEN `the day on which the first fees regulations come into force` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the review took place` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141 CMOPA 6(3B) the review took place within the 30 months` MEANS
    `the day on which the review took place` AT MOST `s 141 CMOPA 6(3B) the last day of the 30 months beginning with the day the first fees regulations come into force` `the day on which the first fees regulations come into force`

DECLARE `s 141 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 141 review the effect of the first fees regulations`

@ref s 141 CMOPA 6(3A)-(3B) (src:2537-2538)
GIVEN `the day on which the first fees regulations come into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `s 141 act`
`s 141 the duty to review the effect of the first fees regulations` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary of State`
    MUST `s 141 review the effect of the first fees regulations`
    WITHIN (Day (`s 141 CMOPA 6(3B) the last day of the 30 months beginning with the day the first fees regulations come into force` `the day on which the first fees regulations come into force`)) MINUS (Day `the day on which the first fees regulations come into force`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary of State` BECAUSE "the review did not take place within the 30 months"

-- CMOPA 6(3C)-(3D): after the review the Secretary of State must make and publish a report containing the conclusions of
-- the review and a statement of what is proposed, and must lay it before Parliament. No time limit is stated.
-- src:2539 | (3C) After the review, the Secretary of State must make and publish a report containing—
-- src:2540 | (a) the conclusions of the review, and
-- src:2541 | (b) a statement as to what the Secretary of State proposes to do in view of those conclusions.
-- src:2542 | (3D) The report must be laid before Parliament by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 141 CMOPA 6(3C)-(3D) (src:2539-2542)
GIVEN `the report contains the conclusions of the review` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report contains a statement as to what the Secretary of State proposes to do in view of those conclusions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report has been laid before Parliament by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141 CMOPA 6(3C)-(3D) the Secretary of State has done what the report provisions require` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the report contains the conclusions of the review`
           AND `the report contains a statement as to what the Secretary of State proposes to do in view of those conclusions`
           AND `the report has been laid before Parliament by the Secretary of State`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsections say what the report "must" contain and that it "must be laid", and give no consequence and no time limit
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

