§ `s 144 Use of jobcentres by sex industry`

-- ETA 2A(2): employment is for sexual purposes if (a) it involves the employee engaging in an activity, and (b) the
-- employee's activity, or the way in which it is performed, may reasonably be assumed to be intended solely or
-- principally to stimulate one or more other persons sexually (by whatever means).
-- src:2555 | (2) For the purposes of this section employment is for sexual purposes if—
-- src:2556 | (a) it involves the employee engaging in an activity, and
-- src:2557 | (b) the employee's activity, or the way in which it is performed, may reasonably be assumed to be intended solely or principally to stimulate one or more other persons sexually (by whatever means).
@ref s 144 ETA 2A(2) (src:2555-2557)
GIVEN `the employment involves the employee engaging in an activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee's activity, or the way in which it is performed, may reasonably be assumed to be intended solely or principally to stimulate one or more other persons sexually` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144 ETA 2A(2) the employment is employment for sexual purposes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the employment involves the employee engaging in an activity`
           AND `the employee's activity, or the way in which it is performed, may reasonably be assumed to be intended solely or principally to stimulate one or more other persons sexually`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "employment is for sexual purposes if (a) it involves the employee engaging in an activity, and (b) ..." a limb fails (a failed "if": a lawyer's reading (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- ETA 2A(1): arrangements made by the Secretary of State under section 2 may not include arrangements in respect of
-- employment for sexual purposes. (3): the Secretary of State may by order specify exceptions to subsection (1).
-- src:2554 | (1) Arrangements made by the Secretary of State under section 2 may not include arrangements in respect of employment for sexual purposes.
@ref s 144 ETA 2A(1) (src:2554)
GIVEN `the employment is employment for sexual purposes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an order under subsection (3) specifies an exception to subsection (1) that covers the employment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144 ETA 2A(1) the arrangements under section 2 are not barred from including arrangements in respect of the employment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the employment is employment for sexual purposes`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `an order under subsection (3) specifies an exception to subsection (1) that covers the employment`
        -- the exception lifts the bar: "The Secretary of State may by order specify exceptions to subsection (1)" (subsection (3))
        WHEN JUST TRUE  THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Arrangements made by the Secretary of State under section 2 may not include arrangements in respect of employment for sexual purposes"
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an order specifies an exception is not among the sources
        WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the employment is for sexual purposes has not been determined
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
